        <Param val="The experiment is now finished.&amp;#10;The goal of this experiment was to compare reaction times and accuracy when people see real words, made up nonwords, and transposed letter nonwords. A transposed letter nonword is a string of letters that closly resembles a real word, but swaps two internal letters. For instance, you might’ve seen “forogt”, but at a glance you might’ve recognized it as “forgot” and answered before your brain could process the misspelling.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Press SPACE to continue." valType="str" updates="constant" name="text" />
